        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="updated">Razarion &middot; last updated 4 September 2026</p>
    </div>

    <p>Razarion is a free, nonprofit, open-source browser game run as a hobby project by Beat
        Keller. By playing it you agree to what follows. It is deliberately short.</p>

    <h2>1. What you get</h2>
    <p>Access to the game, free of charge, for as long as it runs. There is nothing to buy: no
        subscription, no paid currency, no advertising. Crystals and inventory items are earned by
        playing and have no monetary value.</p>

    <h2>2. Your account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You may play without an account. If you create one, keep your password to yourself
            &mdash; anything done through your account counts as done by you.</li>
        <li>Give a working email address. It is the only way to recover a lost password.</li>
        <li>One person, one account. Extra accounts used to gain an advantage in the shared world
            may be removed.</li>
        <li>You may delete your account at any time by writing to the address below.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How to behave</h2>
    <p>Razarion is one persistent world shared by everyone playing it. Do not:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>modify, automate or otherwise manipulate the game client to gain an advantage;</li>
        <li>attack, overload or probe the servers, or interfere with anyone else's game;</li>
        <li>choose a player name that is abusive, hateful, or impersonates someone else;</li>
        <li>use the game to distribute unlawful content.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Accounts that do these things can be suspended or removed. For a free game with a shared
        world, this is the only enforcement there is.</p>

    <h2>4. What the game does not promise</h2>
    <div class="note">
        Razarion is provided as it is, with no warranty of any kind. It may be offline, lose
        progress, change its rules, or stop existing.
    </div>
    <p>It is a hobby project, not a service with a support contract. The world is rebalanced as the
        game develops: units, levels, quests and costs change, and progress earned under older rules
        is not guaranteed to survive. To the extent the law allows, no liability is accepted for any
        loss arising from using the game &mdash; and nothing here limits liability for intent or
        gross negligence.</p>

    <h2>5. Content and code</h2>
    <p>The game's source code is public at
        <a href="https://github.com/Razarion/razarion" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/Razarion/razarion</a>
        under the licence stated there. The name Razarion, the artwork and the game assets remain
        with their authors and are not covered by that licence.</p>
    <p>Recordings and screenshots of your own play are yours to publish freely.</p>

    <h2>6. Data</h2>
    <p>What the game stores and why is set out in the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which is part of these terms.</p>

    <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
